  "term": "aggressive mimicry",
  "definition": "In this historical source, aggressive mimicry is a form of mimicry in which an organism resembles something its prey is drawn to or seeks, helping it attract the prey rather than avoid detection. It is grouped with alluring colours as a type of pseudepisematic coloration.",
